---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import AiDisclosure from '../components/editorial/AiDisclosure.astro';
---
<Base title="How this is made" description="How AI agents write, illustrate, build and review Stay Current, and where human direction fits in.">
  <div class="making-page">
    <header>
      <AiDisclosure />
      <h1>How this is made</h1>
      <p>Stay Current is created with AI, under human direction. AI agents write articles, create illustrations and interactive examples, and build the website.</p>
    </header>

    <section aria-labelledby="direction">
      <h2 id="direction">Human direction</h2>
      <p>The person running Stay Current chooses the subjects, sets the editorial direction, gives feedback and decides what to publish. Human direction does not mean that every article or claim has been reviewed by a person.</p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="reviews">
      <h2 id="reviews">Reviews by AI agents</h2>
      <p>The editorial process assigns separate AI agents to review the work. These reviewers check explanations, source support, examples, figures and writing, then request or make corrections. References to agent review on this site mean review by AI agents.</p>
      <p>Other checks include consulting primary sources, running examples and experiments, and checking page structure and links. The checks vary with the subject; a local teaching model does not establish how a hosted service behaves.</p>
      <p>AI reviewers can miss mistakes or repeat the writer’s assumptions. An article can complete this review process without a person editing it. Review does not guarantee accuracy.</p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="labels">
      <h2 id="labels">What the label means</h2>
      <p>The AI-generated label discloses AI’s role in producing the content. It covers the writing and supporting material, including illustrations and interactive examples. Human direction and edits may also shape the result.</p>
      <p>We use the European Commission’s basic AI icon alongside a plain-language label. The icon identifies AI involvement; it is not a mark of EU approval or a certification of accuracy. The Commission makes the <a href="https://digital-strategy.ec.europa.eu/en/policies/eu-icons-labelling-ai-generated-content">icons and their usage guidance</a> freely available.</p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="editorial-disclaimer">
      <h2 id="editorial-disclaimer">Editorial disclaimer</h2>
      <p>Stay Current is for learning and evaluating engineering choices. AI-generated explanations, figures and examples can contain errors or become outdated as products change. Before applying a procedure or design to a live system, check the primary documentation for the product and version you use, and test the behaviour in your own environment. Do not rely on this site as the sole basis for a production decision.</p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="corrections">
      <h2 id="corrections">Checking a claim or reporting a mistake</h2>
      <p>You can inspect the <a href="https://github.com/ryannel/staycurrent">site’s source and review records</a> or <a href="https://github.com/ryannel/staycurrent/issues/new">report a mistake on GitHub</a>. Include the page address, the passage or example, and what you think needs correcting.</p>
    </section>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .making-page { max-width: 43rem; padding: 1.5rem 0 3rem; }
  header :global(.ai-disclosure) { margin: 0 0 .25rem; font-size: .8rem; font-weight: 600; }
  h1 { font-size: clamp(2.2rem, 5vw, 3.4rem); line-height: 1.13; margin: .5rem 0 1rem; }
  h2 { font-size: 1.6rem; margin-top: 2.5rem; }
</style>
